# 'RA---TPV-SIP' (explicit suffix): the TPV solution of the real ATLAS
# header (real_atlas_k2_tpv, its cards copied: CRPIX ~4000 px off the
# 100x100 stamp) PLUS a SIP set that is NOT a copy of the TPV correction
# (synthetic: 0.4-2 px over the stamp, a residual correction on top of
# TPV). The suffix declares both, so both apply, SIP before the matrix and
# TPV after it, as in wcslib 8.10, which accepts this CTYPE (its golden is
# this case's). TestTPVSIPSuffixAppliesBoth checks the answer moves off
# real_atlas_k2_tpv's by the SIP amount. No AP/BP: hdr2sky injects
# identity AP/BP for wcslib, which inverts by iterating on A/B (as we do).
NOTE pipeline: RA---TPV-SIP with a non-redundant SIP: SIP then TPV
GRID 1 100 12 1 100 12
PIX 50.5 50.5
HEADER
CTYPE1  = 'RA---TPV-SIP'
CTYPE2  = 'DEC--TPV-SIP'
